# Workplace-agnostic skills

This repository’s committed skills are **workplace-agnostic**. Employer-specific skills belong under `workplace-specific/<employer>/` (gitignored except `.gitkeep`).

When adding or editing files under `skills/`:

- Do **not** include employer names, internal hostnames, product names, repo names, or ticket prefixes from a specific workplace
- Do **not** hard-code machine paths, internal MCP plugins, or “how we run tests here” as the only procedure
- Examples and sample commit/PR/ticket text must use generic placeholders (`KEY-123`, `Acme`, `IdP`), not a real workplace’s keys or types

```markdown
# ❌ BAD — workplace leaked into a committed skill
[GOOGLE-8585] - Refactor Data onto GOOGLE gcp model
AWS-11888: sign in via AWS Identity
```

```markdown
# ✅ GOOD — same idea, no workplace
[KEY-123] - Move data onto the shared data model
KEY-123: sign in via the identity provider
```

If the content only makes sense at one employer, put it in `workplace-specific/` instead of `skills/`.
